---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import LegalIdentity from '../../components/LegalIdentity.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, LAST_UPDATED, LEGAL, SITE_NAMES, SITE_URL } from '../../data/site-config';
import { route } from '../../i18n/routes';
const lang = 'en';
---
<PageLayout title={`Privacy policy of ${SITE_NAMES[lang]}: your inputs stay in your browser`} description="What this sales tax and property tax calculator processes: no cookies, no personal data kept by us, only server logs and anonymous stability monitoring. Your US and EU rights." lang={lang} noindex={true} breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Privacy' }]} showAuthor={false}>
  <div class="prose prose-slate max-w-none prose-headings:font-serif">
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
    <p>This policy covers {SITE_URL}. The publisher is established in France, so the EU General Data Protection Regulation applies to everything the site does, whoever the visitor is. Visitors in US states with a consumer privacy law (California and others) have at least the rights described below.</p>
    <h2>1. Controller</h2>
    <LegalIdentity lang={lang} />
    <h2>2. What the calculators never send</h2>
    <p>Prices, local rates, home values, mill rates and states you enter are processed in your browser only. They are not sent to a server, not stored by us and not linked to you. The share link writes your inputs into the page address: only send it to people you choose.</p>
    <h2>3. What is processed</h2>
    <h3>Server logs</h3><p>The host records the IP address, time, page requested and browser, for security. Legal basis: legitimate interest. Retention: according to GitHub's policy.</p>
    <h3>Anonymous stability monitoring with Microsoft Clarity, no cookies</h3><p>The publisher records no personal data about you. To keep the site working, it uses Microsoft Clarity (Microsoft Ireland Operations Limited, One Microsoft Place, Dublin) in cookie-free mode: for each page view, errors, loading times, clicks that lead nowhere and scrolling are measured without any cookie and without linking visits, with page content and inputs masked. Microsoft receives the technical data of the request, including the IP address from which an approximate location is derived, and keeps recordings for 30 days and aggregated data for up to 13 months. Legal basis: legitimate interest in a site that works (Article 6(1)(f) GDPR); no cookie or identifier is kept on your device. You can object at any time by blocking clarity.ms or by writing to us. There is no advertising.</p>
    <h3>E-mails</h3><p>If you write to us, your address and message are kept to answer you, for three years after the last exchange.</p>
    <h2>4. Sale or sharing of personal information</h2><p>We do not sell or share personal information, for money or otherwise, and we do not use it for targeted advertising. Microsoft receives technical monitoring data only to provide that service to us.</p>
    <h2>5. Recipients and transfers</h2><p>The host, GitHub, Inc., and Microsoft, for the stability monitoring, are in the United States; data may be processed there under the EU–US Data Privacy Framework.</p>
    <h2>6. Your rights</h2><p>Access, correction, deletion, restriction, objection and portability: write to <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>; we reply within one month. You can complain to the {LEGAL.supervisoryAuthority} (<a href={LEGAL.supervisoryAuthorityUrl} rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">{LEGAL.supervisoryAuthorityUrl}</a>).</p>
    <h2>7. Children</h2><p>The site is not directed at children under 13 and collects nothing from them.</p>
    <p>See also the <a href={route('cookies', lang)}>cookies page</a>. Updated: {LAST_UPDATED}.</p>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
